requirements.detail:
Adhesion strength at joint interfaces must comply with strict limits: 
a) Kids: Upper to sole/midsole/composite sole and interlayer bond must be minimum 1.0 N/mm (or 1.0 N/mm in case of material tear); 
b) Adults (Type 1): Upper to sole/midsole/composite sole and interlayer bond must be minimum 2.5 N/mm (or 2.0 N/mm in case of material tear); 
c) Adults (Type 2): Upper to sole/midsole/composite sole and interlayer bond must be minimum 1.5 N/mm (or 1.0 N/mm in case of material tear).

Constituent materials (uppers, linings, outsoles) must comply with the strict environmental and toxicity limits specified in IS 17011: 
a) Allergenic & carcinogenic disperse dyes: < 1 mg/l; 
b) Aromatic amines from Azo dyes: < 20 mg/kg; 
c) Chromium (VI) in leather parts: < 3 mg/kg; 
d) Dimethyl fumarate (DMFu): < 0.1 mg/kg; 
e) Formaldehyde: Kids < 20 mg/kg; Adults (direct skin contact) < 75 mg/kg; Adults (no direct contact) < 100 mg/kg; 
f) Organotin compounds (TBT/TPhT): < 1 mg/kg; other organotins (DBT/DOT/MBT/MOT): < 5 mg/kg each; 
g) Phthalates: strictly restricted per individual compounds.
